{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "db6269e5-4e10-421f-a812-809e08979e32",
    "name": "Blotato Comment Service — /v2",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "description": "Retrieve comments for a published post, and reply to a comment. Every request asserts an HTTP status and, on failure, the exact error.code + error.reason.\n\nSETUP\n1. Import this file into Postman.\n2. baseUrl defaults to the live demo. To hit a local instance, edit the collection variable to http://localhost:3000.\n3. Run \"List comments — tenant A\" first: it captures {{commentId}} and {{cursor}} that the Reply folder chains off.\n4. Or use the Collection Runner top-to-bottom — folders are ordered so state is populated before it is used.\n\nNOTE Reply requests publish through the deployment's configured provider and create data; that is expected and safe against the demo/fixture provider. Auth follows assumption A-001: the X-Account-Id header is the tenant context supplied by the platform gateway."
  },
